<h1>ZeParty PK Battle & Agora RTC: Backend Developer Technical Handoff Report</h1>
<p><strong>System:</strong> ZeParty Backend API & Socket Services<br>
<strong>Feature:</strong> Real-time PK Cross-Room Video Battle (Host & Audience)<br>
<strong>Target Audience:</strong> Backend Engineering Team<br>
<strong>Date:</strong> 4 November 2026<br>
<strong>Status:</strong> <span class='badge badge-info'>BACKEND SPECIFICATION & INTEGRATION REQUIREMENTS</span></p>

<hr/>

<h2>1. Executive Summary</h2>
<p>The Flutter mobile frontend has been updated to support full dual-stream cross-room Agora RTC live video rendering for PK matches using Agora multi-channel client-side subscription (<code>joinChannelEx</code>). Both hosts and audience members in Room A and Room B now stream the local room host directly and subscribe to the opponent room's Agora channel.</p>
<p>To ensure 100% operational reliability in production, this report details the exact API endpoints, token issuance policies, socket broadcasts, and metadata contracts that the backend must strictly maintain and verify.</p>

<h2>2. Core Architecture Overview: How Frontend Uses Agora in PK</h2>
<div class='alert-box'>
<p><strong>Connection Topology:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Primary Channel:</strong> User connects to their local room channel (e.g. <code>room_7ce19563...</code>) using the main Agora engine session. Host publishes camera and audio as <code>BROADCASTER</code>; audience subscribes as <code>AUDIENCE</code>.</li>
<li><strong>Secondary Cross-Room Channel:</strong> When a PK battle starts, the client calls <code>POST /v1/rooms/:id/agora-token</code> with the <strong>opponent's room ID</strong>. The client then joins the opponent's channel using <code>joinChannelEx</code> with <code>clientRoleAudience</code>, subscribing to the opponent host's video and audio stream.</li>
</ul>
</div>

<h2>3. Required Backend API Specifications & Contracts</h2>

<h3>3.1. Token Generation Endpoint: <code>POST /v1/rooms/:id/agora-token</code></h3>
<p>When a client in Room A subscribes to Room B's live video stream, it requests an Agora token for Room B.</p>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Field / Rule</th>
<th>Required Backend Behavior</th>
<th>Critical Importance</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><strong>Cross-Room Authorization</strong></td>
<td>Allow active users to request a token for <code>:id</code> (the opponent room) even if they are not listed in that room's seat list or regular member array.</td>
<td><span class='badge badge-crit'>BLOCKING</span> If backend restricts token generation only to seated participants or members who performed a full room join, cross-room PK video subscription will fail with HTTP 403.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Assigned Role</strong></td>
<td>Assign <code>AGORA_ROLES.AUDIENCE</code> (Subscriber) for cross-room token requests, since the visiting user only consumes the opponent stream and does not publish to the opponent channel.</td>
<td><span class='badge badge-pass'>APPROVED</span> Prevents unauthorized audio/video injection into the opponent's room.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Deterministic UID</strong></td>
<td>Must use <code>deriveAgoraUid(userId)</code>. The generated integer UID must remain deterministic across all rooms.</td>
<td><span class='badge badge-crit'>BLOCKING</span> In Agora RTC Engine v6+, the <code>localUid</code> passed in <code>RtcConnection</code> must match the UID signed into the token.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Channel Name Consistency</strong></td>
<td>Must always return the authoritative <code>channelName</code> (e.g. <code>room_<id_without_hyphens></code>), never <code>null</code> or raw UUID with hyphens.</td>
<td><span class='badge badge-crit'>BLOCKING</span> Agora project certificate enforces exact string matching on channel names.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Token Expiration</strong></td>
<td>Minimum expiry should be <strong>3600 seconds</strong> (1 hour). Standard PK match duration is 180 to 300 seconds.</td>
<td><span class='badge badge-warn'>HIGH</span> Avoids token expiration mid-match during intense battles.</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>

<h4>Expected Success Response Format:</h4>
<pre>
{
  "success": true,
  "message": "Agora RTC token generated successfully.",
  "data": {
    "token": "007eJxTYJj7...",
    "channelName": "room_c2c1649cd26145608ae39df1e9ea8e7b",
    "uid": 9202535,
    "appId": "970ca35de60c44645bbae8a215061401",
    "expiresIn": 3600
  }
}
</pre>

<hr/>

<h3>3.2. PK Battle Object & <code>agoraRelay</code> Metadata</h3>
<p>All endpoints returning PK match data (including <code>POST /v1/pk/create</code>, <code>POST /v1/pk/start</code>, <code>POST /v1/pk/join</code>, <code>GET /v1/pk/matches/active/:roomId</code>) and socket events must include the authoritative <code>agoraRelay</code> object.</p>

<h4>Required Structure of <code>agoraRelay</code>:</h4>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Property</th>
<th>Type</th>
<th>Description</th>
<th>Example Value</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><code>channelA</code></td>
<td>String</td>
<td>Agora channel name of Room A (host A's room)</td>
<td><code>"room_7ce1956331724a0b9df6b6aa6b57db45"</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>channelB</code></td>
<td>String</td>
<td>Agora channel name of Room B (host B's room)</td>
<td><code>"room_c2c1649cd26145608ae39df1e9ea8e7b"</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>hostAUid</code></td>
<td>Integer (32-bit)</td>
<td>Authoritative Agora UID of Host A (derived via <code>deriveAgoraUid</code>)</td>
<td><code>9202535</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>hostBUid</code></td>
<td>Integer (32-bit)</td>
<td>Authoritative Agora UID of Host B (derived via <code>deriveAgoraUid</code>)</td>
<td><code>2643319</code></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>

<div class='alert-box'>
<p><strong>Note for Backend:</strong> In <code>backend/src/repositories/pk.repository.js#L1049-L1054</code>, this is already defined as:</p>
<pre>
agoraRelay: {
  channelA: match.roomA?.agoraChannelName || match.roomAId,
  channelB: match.roomB?.agoraChannelName || match.roomBId,
  hostAUid: deriveAgoraUid(match.hostAUserId),
  hostBUid: deriveAgoraUid(match.hostBUserId),
}
</pre>
<p><strong>Required Verification:</strong> Ensure <code>match.roomA.agoraChannelName</code> and <code>match.roomB.agoraChannelName</code> are never null. If null, automatically populate with <code>room_${match.roomAId.replace(/-/g, '')}</code> before saving and returning.</p>
</div>

<hr/>

<h2>4. Socket.IO Event Broadcasting Requirements</h2>
<p>PK Battles involve two distinct rooms (Room A and Room B). All PK socket events <strong>MUST be broadcast to BOTH rooms simultaneously</strong>.</p>

<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Event Name</th>
<th>Broadcast Scope</th>
<th>Payload Requirements</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><code>pk:started</code></td>
<td>Emit to <code>roomAId</code> AND <code>roomBId</code></td>
<td>Full <code>PKBattleModel</code> JSON including <code>id</code>, <code>roomAId</code>, <code>roomBId</code>, <code>hostA</code>, <code>hostB</code>, <code>durationSeconds</code>, <code>startedAt</code>, and <code>agoraRelay</code>.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>pk:score_update</code></td>
<td>Emit to <code>roomAId</code> AND <code>roomBId</code></td>
<td><code>{ "battleId": "...", "scoreA": 1500, "scoreB": 2200 }</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>pk:ended</code> / <code>pk:finished</code></td>
<td>Emit to <code>roomAId</code> AND <code>roomBId</code></td>
<td>Final scores, winner user/side ID, MVP supporter data.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>pk:aborted</code> / <code>pk:forfeited</code></td>
<td>Emit to <code>roomAId</code> AND <code>roomBId</code></td>
<td>Reason for abort (e.g. host disconnected, forfeit).</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>

<hr/>

<h2>5. Room Reconnect & Active Match Recovery: <code>GET /v1/pk/matches/active/:roomId</code></h2>
<p>When an audience member enters a room that is already in the middle of a PK match, or when a host app crashes/reconnects, the mobile frontend queries:</p>
<code>GET /v1/pk/matches/active/:roomId</code>

<h3>Backend Verification Rules:</h3>
<ol>
<li>The query must return the currently active match where <code>(roomAId == :roomId OR roomBId == :roomId) AND status == 'STARTED' AND endedAt IS NULL</code>.</li>
<li>Calculate remaining duration: <code>remainingSeconds = durationSeconds - floor((now - startedAt) / 1000)</code>. If expired, update status to <code>FINISHED</code>.</li>
<li>Must include the complete <code>agoraRelay</code> metadata object.</li>
</ol>

<hr/>

